WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.761
The day arrived to start our journey to visit the squire's friends.

2
00:00:05.762 --> 00:00:10.882
John and James hitched Ginger and me to the carriage.

3
00:00:10.883 --> 00:00:17.229
Then James drove us to the front doors of the house where the squire and his wife were waiting.

4
00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:21.785
They got in, and we were off.

5
00:00:21.786 --> 00:00:24.055
We were on the road all day.

6
00:00:24.056 --> 00:00:28.900
There were some steep hills along the way, but James drove very carefully.

7
00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:34.225
And he always kept us on the smoothest part of the road.

8
00:00:34.226 --> 00:00:39.752
If the uphill was long, he turned the carriage to the side to let us rest for a moment.

9
00:00:39.753 --> 00:00:46.826
Ginger and I were grateful for his thoughtfulness. It made our job easier.

10
00:00:46.827 --> 00:00:50.950
Just as the sun was going down, we reached a town.

11
00:00:50.951 --> 00:00:54.154
"We'll stop here for the night," the squire said.

12
00:00:54.155 --> 00:00:57.370
"Take us to the hotel, please, James."

13
00:00:57.371 --> 00:00:59.864
"Yes, sir," James said.

14
00:00:59.865 --> 00:01:06.125
He drove us through the streets and beneath an archway that led into the courtyard of a large hotel.

15
00:01:06.126 --> 00:01:12.776
We left the squire and his wife at the entrance, and then continued on to the stables at the back.

16
00:01:12.777 --> 00:01:19.018
A stable worker was waiting for us. He was a little old man with a crooked leg.

17
00:01:19.019 --> 00:01:21.799
But the leg didn't seem to bother him much.

18
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:27.082
He was as active and lively as could be, rushing out to help James unhitch us.

19
00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:30.522
"What a beauty you are," he told me in a friendly voice.

20
00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:35.725
Let's get you cleaned up so you can rest, all right?"

21
00:01:35.726 --> 00:01:39.316
He led me into the stable.

22
00:01:39.317 --> 00:01:44.569
There were a number of stalls in there, with horses standing in several of them.

23
00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.634
Another worker brought Ginger in.

24
00:01:47.635 --> 00:01:51.394
He began to groom her while the little old man worked on me.

25
00:01:51.395 --> 00:01:55.229
James watched them both carefully.

26
00:01:55.230 --> 00:02:01.876
I have never been groomed as lightly and expertly as I was by that little old man.

27
00:02:01.877 --> 00:02:05.846
When he finished, James ran his hands over me.

28
00:02:05.847 --> 00:02:07.907
"Wow," he said.

29
00:02:07.908 --> 00:02:13.462
"I thought I was fast at grooming a horse, and my boss John even faster.

30
00:02:13.463 --> 00:02:16.589
But you put us both to shame!"

31
00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:21.200
"Practice makes perfect," the old man said with a chuckle.

32
00:02:21.201 --> 00:02:27.183
"And I've had plenty of practice. I've been doing this for forty years!"

33
00:02:27.184 --> 00:02:33.838
"Forty years?" James said, sounding impressed. "That's a long time."

34
00:02:33.839 --> 00:02:40.202
"Yes, indeed," the old man agreed. "I started at age twelve.

35
00:02:40.203 --> 00:02:44.387
I've always been small, so I was a jockey for a while.

36
00:02:44.388 --> 00:02:49.449
But one day I was riding in a race when my horse slipped.

37
00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:54.621
I came off and broke my knee, and after that I couldn't ride anymore.

38
00:02:54.622 --> 00:02:59.610
But I couldn't live without horses, so I got a job at this hotel."

39
00:02:59.611 --> 00:03:04.265
"I can see that you do a good job here," James said.

40
00:03:04.266 --> 00:03:07.593
"Thank you, my boy," the old man said.

41
00:03:07.594 --> 00:03:13.180
"I enjoy it, especially when I get the chance to handle an animal like this one."

42
00:03:13.181 --> 00:03:15.404
He patted me.

43
00:03:15.405 --> 00:03:21.827
"If you let me handle a horse for a few minutes, I can always tell you what sort of treatment he's had.

44
00:03:21.828 --> 00:03:29.382
And I can tell this black horse of yours is well-bred and was treated kindly."

45
00:03:29.383 --> 00:03:33.382
After that the old man put me in a stall and fed me.

46
00:03:33.383 --> 00:03:42.089
Ginger was in the stall beside me, and we were both glad to have a rest after our long day on the road.

47
00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:46.802
Later that evening a different worker came in to give us more hay and water.

48
00:03:46.803 --> 00:03:52.756
Horses stood in every stall by now, and he was busy taking care of us all.

49
00:03:52.757 --> 00:03:57.715
Then a young man wandered in. He was smoking a pipe.

50
00:03:57.716 --> 00:04:02.885
"Hello, Fowler," the worker greeted him. "Could you do me a favor?"

51
00:04:02.886 --> 00:04:09.493
"Sure, what is it?" The young man let out a puff of smoke from his pipe.

52
00:04:09.494 --> 00:04:14.477
"Climb up into the loft and toss down some more hay," the worker said.

53
00:04:14.478 --> 00:04:18.440
"But be sure to set down your pipe first."

54
00:04:18.441 --> 00:04:23.321
"All right." The young man hurried off out of sight.

55
00:04:23.322 --> 00:04:27.398
Just then James came into the stable to check on Ginger and me.

56
00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:32.988
"Everything looks fine here," he said, giving us each a pat.

57
00:04:32.989 --> 00:04:39.902
"Get some rest, and I'll see you in the morning."

58
00:04:39.903 --> 00:04:45.683
Shortly after he left, the stable went dark and quiet for the night.

59
00:04:45.684 --> 00:04:50.411
I ate a little more hay, and then drifted off to sleep.

60
00:04:50.412 --> 00:04:54.284
I awoke sometime later, feeling strangely uncomfortable.

61
00:04:54.285 --> 00:04:57.530
At first I wasn't sure why.

62
00:04:57.531 --> 00:05:03.086
I stood, coughing. A moment later Ginger coughed too.

63
00:05:03.087 --> 00:05:09.284
The air was thick with smoke, and a crackling sound came from the loft overhead.

64
00:05:09.285 --> 00:05:15.968
Suddenly there was a cry from somewhere outside: "Fire!"

